For this M2 task, I accept the existing M1 conventions as the engineering reference: decision state after current receipts; nonnegative integer orders; positive fixed lead time L; an order at t first available at t+L; unmet demand is lost, not backlogged; holding cost applies before the next receipt; ordering costs are charged on placement; the finite horizon has zero additional terminal salvage or penalty. Preserve these semantics and the M1 fixtures. This does not establish that these boundaries are final for the publication study.

