Run the existing tests before edits. If the checkout is clean and idle, create a scoped task branch. If it contains pre-existing changes, report them and do not discard, stash or overwrite them. Use the installed environment, one CPU process and bounded tiny examples; keep each test/demo process within 120 seconds. No package installation, dataset download, GPU training, full sweep, destructive cleanup, commit, push or merge is authorized by this prompt.

All canonical source, tests and configs must remain inside ../github. Preserve all raw/processed data and past results. Use synthetic cases for M2; do not use M5 test outcomes or access Favorita. Do not change manuscript prose, claimed contributions or the proposed GP mechanism to make the implementation appear complete.

After implementation, run all relevant tests and the deterministic reference/demo; inspect the diff. Record the actual task approval, assumptions, commands, test outcomes and remaining blockers in the project logs without claiming a theorem or empirical RL result. Leave a reviewable uncommitted diff and propose a commit message.

Your final response must state: what changed; exact commands I can rerun; measured reference/demo results and test outcomes; limitations; branch and dirty/clean status; and the next milestone. Stop at M2 review. Do not continue to M3/M4 or launch any training until I authorize the next task.
